  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Griffiths established a Seattle shipping business serving Pacific Northwest and international routes. Expansion into physical infrastructure followed when he acquired the Winslow Marine Railway and Shipbuilding Company on Bainbridge Island. The yard built and repaired vessels, giving the family enterprise direct control over an important part of maritime operations.\n\nHis interests included both commercial ships and a substantial private motor vessel built at Winslow. The combination reflected an operator’s approach: transport services, shipyard capacity and vessel ownership reinforced one another. The business continued through later generations as James Griffiths & Sons, preserving a regional maritime name. Historical sources vary between Griffiths and Griffeths, but the company and vessel chronology identify the same Seattle captain and industrial proprietor.",
